1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,380
I think you've been acting really strange lately,

3
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:31,740
like you're living in another dimension.

4
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,580
This time, right here, I must

5
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,500
shatter his confidence again.

6
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:40,860
This is my Eastern Intuition style of Yo-Yo.

7
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,260
I will surpass you.

8
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:49,020
What's the point of occasionally tying with me?

9
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Episode 32

10
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,220
Somewhere in the US.

11
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,660
Invincible Eagle

12
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,580
Crimson Holy Light

13
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,500
I just hope you

14
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,420
don't forget the agreement between us.

15
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,700
I arranged for you to join the Saint Qiao Team

16
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:01,980
as its Captain so you can lead the Saint Qiao Team to win

17
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:05,340
the Team Championship of the
Blazing Teens Yo-Yo Tournament.

18
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,740
Don't just focus purely on defeating

19
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,140
Leo for personal reasons.

20
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,020
I don't need your excessive reminders.

21
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,310
You gave me the chance to

22
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:19,560
defeat Leo in an Official Tournament in China.

23
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,980
Of course I won't ignore your request.

24
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,780
Regarding what I've promised,

25
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,140
I will never forget it.

26
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,980
Don't worry.

27
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:41,820
Everything is under my control.

28
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,500
I'm exhausted.

29
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,740
I can't hold on any longer, it's way too hot.

30
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:35,640
Do you want a sip?

31
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,260
Hey, Chuck, I think you almost

32
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,180
look like an overcooked steamed bun.

33
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:48,840
You're slacking off yourself and laughing at others.

34
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:50,940
I can't understand the three of them.

35
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,340
They're as hard working as
an Air Conditioner in the Summer.

36
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,260
Don't even mention Air Conditioners.

37
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,180
Our Air Conditioner is really awful.

38
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:59,580
The hardest thing to endure in life is

39
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,710
an Air Conditioner that's not cold on a scorching day.

40
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,900
Sis, come take a break for a bit.

41
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,820
Everyone, take a break.

42
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:16,380
Hey, Meatball.

43
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,780
Where's the drink sponsored by your Dad?

44
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,700
I'm dying of thirst here.

45
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,620
It should be arriving soon.

46
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,540
I even called him specifically last night

47
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,460
to tell him not to forget.

48
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:27,900
I can't wait anymore.

49
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:29,790
At the rate your Dad's drinks are coming,

50
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,290
I'll probably have died of thirst way before.

51
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:34,620
Where's Leo?

52
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,020
I saw him just a moment ago.

53
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,900
Looks like he went out with Shawn.

54
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,300
Lately, the Captain has been acting really odd.

55
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:45,230
Almost like he's in the same realm as Shawn.

56
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,540
I feel like his head's been in the clouds.

57
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,950
He's always spacing out by himself.

58
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,420
And when you talk to him,

59
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:52,610
his answers don't even make sense.

60
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,300
Is it really that serious?

61
00:05:54,660 --> 00:05:55,850
Maybe he's just too tired.

62
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:57,180
Too tired?

63
00:05:57,920 --> 00:05:59,300
Aren't we all just as tired?

64
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,500
Not only is he distracted,

65
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,900
he's also vanishes suddenly several times.

66
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,300
Look, he's gone again.

67
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:09,180
I think this should count as leaving early.

68
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:13,260
Yeah, I noticed that a while ago too.

69
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,420
Mini, can you go ask him

70
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,340
if something's on his mind?

71
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,780
Alright.

72
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,050
Sis already asked him, but he won't say.

73
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,510
Good job, Team.

74
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,500
How's the Training going?

75
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,700
Everyone seems to be in pretty good shape.

76
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,590
Coach, I want to file a complaint.

77
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,580
This Air Conditioner is not in good shape.

78
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,020
Oh, really?

79
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,860
Look at you, you're all drenched in sweat.

80
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:44,220
Alright, I'll complain to the School right away.

81
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,660
I'll have them send someone to fix it.

82
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,540
You can have some drinks first

83
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,770
to prevent heatstroke.

84
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,340
But Coach,

85
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,300
We don't have any drinks.

86
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:58,620
Oh, I've been so busy all morning,

87
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,560
I completely forgot about it.

88
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:03,390
Actually, Chuck's Dad sent someone over

89
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:05,310
first thing this morning with a ton of drinks.

90
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,500
I put them all in my PE Office.

91
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,940
I'll go grab them for you, alright?

92
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:10,140
Then we'll go get them.

93
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,100
No need, I'll go.

94
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,980
You guys rest up and then train a bit more.

95
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,380
Coach, can you manage all that by yourself?

96
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:18,550
I can manage. Do I look that old?

97
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:20,250
Can't I even carry a few crates of drinks?

98
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,140
Go on, train.

99
00:07:25,660 --> 00:07:26,940
Alright, let's continue Training, everyone.

100
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:04,860
What was that?

101
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:05,820
Lets check it out!

102
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:09,180
Coach!

103
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Yes.

104
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:25,980
Jacky!

105
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,900
How's your Investigation going?

106
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:33,180
What? Coach Tony fell and got injured?

107
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,420
Coach,

108
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,830
if you had let us go get the drinks,

109
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,820
wouldn't it have been fine?

110
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:44,220
If you'd been the ones hit and injured,

111
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:45,420
that would've been even worse.

112
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:49,500
Chuck, your Dad's people are so clumsy,

113
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,940
stacking things up so high.

114
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,600
Couldn't they have just laid them out on the floor?

115
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:56,700
You can't blame my Dad for this.

116
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,540
The Competition is just around the corner.

117
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,460
What are we going to do now, Coach?

118
00:09:03,880 --> 00:09:07,740
First, don't panic. Stay calm. Understand?

119
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,980
Coach, the Doctor said it's better to
be hospitalized for a fracture.

120
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:15,900
I'd rather stay at home.

121
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:17,820
I'm not used to Hospitals.

122
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,740
Besides, this is no big deal,

123
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,180
as long as I don't move it around.

124
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:24,060
They say a broken bone takes 100 days to heal.

125
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,320
It won't get better anytime soon.

126
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:29,820
Coach,

127
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,940
for future Training, I'll come to you daily for Instructions,

128
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,460
and then report back to you.

129
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:38,460
No...

130
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:39,710
No need for all that trouble.

131
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:41,340
Leo,

132
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,780
from today onward,

133
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,230
all Jianghai Teams' Training and Matches

134
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,400
are your full responsibility.

135
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,940
You'll independently take on this responsibility.

136
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:51,900
Coach.

137
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,140
I... I'm afraid this won't work.

138
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,060
There's nothing that won't work.

139
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,460
I believe in you. You can definitely do it.

140
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:06,780
When you all go back,

141
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:10,140
make sure to refine your Signature Moves
with even more precision,

142
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:12,260
and follow the Captain's Instructions.

143
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:17,340
Understand?

144
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,260
Yes, understood.

145
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,470
Don't let an Incident like today's

146
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,460
throw us into disarray.

147
00:10:27,400 --> 00:10:29,340
Nothing in life ever goes completely smoothly.

148
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,660
You need to learn to adjust your mindset and plans

149
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:36,060
promptly in the face of unexpected changes.

150
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,940
This is also a great form of Training.

151
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:42,780
Leo.

152
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,220
What do you have to say?

153
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:51,900
I... I'm still worried I can't shoulder this burden.

154
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,060
There's nothing to worry about.

155
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,320
Just go ahead and do it.

156
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,900
The Jianghai Team is in your hands now.

157
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,730
Anyone else have something to say?

158
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:38,460
The Coach isn't here.

159
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,380
How are we supposed to compete with them?

160
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,780
Don't say such discouraging things.

161
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,180
This is the most critical moment.

162
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:48,060
Everyone should encourage each other and unite as one.

163
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:51,900
Leo, what do you think?

164
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,220
I have something to do.

165
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,620
I've got to go first. Bye.

166
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,020
Leo!

167
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:19,740
Some Captain he is. What kind of attitude is that?

168
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
I'll go check on him.

169
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,100
Let me go check on him.

170
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:27,900
Let's go.

171
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,500
Mini

172
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,300
You should go talk to Leo.

173
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:58,140
He might be under too much pressure.

174
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,060
I have a great idea.

175
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,460
I suggest he eat my Dad's Fish Head Casserole.

176
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,860
Maybe it'll relieve some of that pressure.

177
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,820
Oh, please.

178
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,220
Quit advertising for your Dad.

179
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,540
The hardest thing to endure in life is

180
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,470
your Dad's Fish Head Casserole.

181
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:15,930
That's crossing the line.

182
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,730
Didn't you drink the whole pot

183
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:20,060
of Fish Head Soup last time?

184
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,140
Huh, I only took a tiny sip.

185
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,060
Matthew drank the rest.

186
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:29,340
Well... Chuck's Dad was treating us, so...

187
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,700
Let's go.

188
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,260
Guys, look over there!

189
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,360
That looks like Jacky!

190
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:46,140
That person next to Jacky

191
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,580
doesn't seem to be from the Chengnan Team.

192
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,940
But he looks really familiar,

193
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,300
Like I've seen him before.

194
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,380
Yes! He's the Masked Guy from the Falcon Base.

195
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:06,300
That's right, it's him.

196
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:09,180
I suspected the Chengnan Team was
behind it from the start.

197
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:12,540
Jacky not only denied it, he even mocked me.

198
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,140
Let's get out of here.

199
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,900
What are you afraid of? A bunch of rookies.

200
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:33,180
Hey, why aren't you wearing your Mask today?

201
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:36,540
I think you look much cooler with the Mask on.

202
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,940
You'd look awesome walking around town with a Mask on.

203
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:42,300
What are you guys talking about?
Cousin, let's go.

204
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,620
Ah, so the Mysterious Guy is his Cousin!

205
00:14:46,650 --> 00:14:47,580
Don't move!

206
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,380
Why should we leave?

207
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:56,220
If they think I'm Mysterious, let them think that.

208
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:58,340
Being Mysterious isn't against the law.

209
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:01,020
Well, your 'Mystery' was totally despicable!

210
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,660
And completely shameless, you know that?

211
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:03,900
You're the despicable ones.

212
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,260
What, trying to overpower us with numbers?

213
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,180
Back at the Falcon Base,

214
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:11,100
you sent this Mysterious Guy to attack us.

215
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,730
What does that prove?

216
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,900
Hey, you should have some evidence when you say things.

217
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,820
He's my Cousin.

218
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:21,180
What does that have to do with some Mysterious Person?

219
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:22,140
Of course we have evidence.

220
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:23,580
I recognized him.

221
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,500
When you snatched my Yo-Yo,

222
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,900
you used the exact same move you just did!

223
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:32,700
Hmph, anyone on the street can do that move.

224
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:35,100
See? I can do it too.

225
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,460
Hey, little chubby.

226
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,820
Your attempt at that move was pathetic.

227
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:46,620
When I beat you, I did it way cooler.

228
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,860
Jacky, just stop pretending.

229
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,300
Your Cousin already confessed.

230
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:55,740
What are you still denying?

231
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:56,900
Who's denying?

232
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,440
Why should we be afraid of them?

233
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,020
They're all just a bunch of Losers I've already beaten!

234
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,860
Fine, let me tell you all something.

235
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:08,220
Back then, my Cousin was on summer break.

236
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,100
I invited him to come and mess with you guys a little.

237
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,980
Just to teach you a little lesson.

238
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:17,770
To show you that there's always someone better out there.

239
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:18,980
Always another mountain to climb.

240
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:20,700
Mask Guy.

241
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,620
I hate it when people play dirty tricks on me.

242
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,500
Today, let's settle this fair and square.

243
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:31,740
Fine, I accept your challenge.

244
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,140
You pick the place.

245
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Come on.

246
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:44,220
Flying Dragon To The Moon!

247
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:49,020
Golden Dragon Tail Whip!

248
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:19,260
Wow!

249
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,300
Nice

250
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,540
Awesome!

251
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,340
You've improved so fast.

252
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:30,780
I'm flattered.

253
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,180
But I think losing fair and square

254
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,580
is way better than winning by sneaky means.

255
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:42,300
Cousin, looks like I can't help you out anymore.

256
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,620
You'll just have to settle your
scores on the Tournament stage.

257
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,460
Everyone.

258
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:52,860
We'll meet again.

259
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:55,260
Cousin!

260
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:00,060
See you at the Tournament!

261
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,980
Alright, it's settled then.

262
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:06,300
We finally got to vent our anger.

263
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:09,660
The Captain is still as dominant as ever.

264
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:12,540
His momentum is unstoppable, his power just like before.

265
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:15,900
Old but still sharp!

266
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:17,820
What kind of nonsense are you guys spouting?

267
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:23,580
Bro, you're making it way too obvious!

268
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:28,860
Teddy, your acting is terrible.

269
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,180
How could you be so careless?

270
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:54,780
Who injures their own leg just carrying drinks?

271
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,180
I guess it's just like the old saying goes.

272
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,580
"Shooting yourself in your own foot."

273
00:20:00,390 --> 00:20:02,940
Still joking around at your age?

274
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,300
Be more careful from now on.

275
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:07,740
Now that your leg is injured,

276
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:09,380
who's going to take care of you?

277
00:20:10,390 --> 00:20:11,100
I'm fine

278
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:15,900
I'm managing.

279
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:17,820
And how have you been lately?

280
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:22,620
Me? I can still jump around, way better than you.

281
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:26,910
But that doesn't mean your Team is stronger

282
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,900
than my Team, right?

283
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,260
Oh, stop it. You just love
showing off in front of me.

284
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,380
Come on, eat up.

285
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:48,240
There's plenty.

286
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:57,660
Smells great. You've learned to cook now?

287
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:00,540
That's quite an Achievement.

288
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,900
Looks like you're getting ready to be a bride.

289
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,490
Don't talk nonsense, or I'll get mad.

290
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,270
Don't,

291
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,580
I was just trying to cheer you up.

292
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:16,860
Seriously, though,

293
00:21:17,020 --> 00:21:17,820
you should seriously consider

294
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:19,740
finding someone to take care of you.

